// ── SKIN-METALLED VARIANTS (2026-08-28, Jeff: "make the crew/compass/2d/3d glyphs
// change with the silver/gold skins") ───────────────────────────────────────────
// CarPlay cannot TINT a template button — Apple owns that colour. But these are our
// own pixels delivered as data URIs, so the metal is simply baked in. Three sets of
// the same silhouettes; nothing about sizing, padding or `scale` changes.
//
// HOW THEY WERE MADE (and the trap that shaped it): the H-logo bake on 2026-08-23
// ramped RGB toward white and came out desaturated. So the restyler works in HSV and
// TRANSPLANTS the lighting instead: for each pixel it reads where the pixel sits along
// the SOURCE (green) ramp by inverse-interpolating its VALUE, takes that pixel's local
// deviation from the flat ramp — which IS the gloss band, the bright top edge and the
// dark rim — then rebuilds from the TARGET ramp at the same position and re-applies the
// deviation. Hue and saturation therefore always come from tierTheme's ramp, never from
// a white ramp, and the shading survives intact.
//
// VERIFIED by pixel-sampling against the SHIPPED H assets (h-gold@3x / h-silver@3x),
// which are themselves faithful to the tierTheme ramps: worst hue deviation 3.2°.
//
// ⚠ THE SILVER COMPASS NEEDED A SPECIAL CASE. Green and gold needles separate from the
// compass's white chrome body by CHROMA (measured Δsat 0.760 / 0.697). Silver IS grey,
// so that separation collapsed to 0.059 and the needle merged into the white half — a
// compass that cannot show you north. Its accent pixels are darkened 42% AFTER the
// lighting transplant (doing it before just inflates the delta and the value climbs
// back: measured 0.121 -> 0.110), which re-separates it by VALUE: Δval 0.223.
//
// ⚠ ANDROID AUTO still flattens all of these to white silhouettes — androidx tints
// MapActionStrip icons and the CarIcon tint override is a NATIVE patch that has never
// landed (nothing in patches/). So this is CarPlay-only until that ships.
//
// Regenerate with tools/glyph-remetal (kept in the OTA commit message).
const CAR_ICON_CREW_PREMIUM: CarIcon = icon(
  '',
);
